      "raw_response": "Option C. The lemming will die.\n\nThis is because lemmings, like most animals, have a high mortality rate in situations that cause them significant physical stress, such as falling from a great height. While the myth that lemmings jump off cliffs in large numbers and follow each other to their deaths has been perpetuated by media and popular culture, there is no scientific evidence to support this claim (Source: National Geographic, \"The Lemming Myth\"). In reality, lemmings are primarily driven by instinct to find suitable habitats and food sources, and their behavior is not influenced by the actions of individual members of their group (Source: Animal Planet, \"Lemming Facts\").\n\nANSWER: C",
